  "fin_note": "<b>With vs. without philanthropy:</b> stripped of grants, August's consolidated operating result (EBITDA) is a <b>loss of $106,653</b> — a miss versus the roughly breakeven forecast (+$803), and about even with a year ago (−$100,435). But YTD the EBITDA loss of <b>$1.36M still beats forecast by $724K</b> and has <b>narrowed ~48% YoY</b> (from −$2.63M). August philanthropy was light — $55,589 vs July's $851K, a grant-timing swing — so adjusted net income was a small <b>−$51,064 for the month</b> yet remains <b>+$1,106,369 YTD</b>. Revenue of $1.76M came in −1.1% to forecast and −9.1% YoY; expenses of $1.87M ran $88K over forecast, driven by the unbudgeted Best of magazine, IT ($42K over, incl. $20K Blue Engine) and printing ($26K over). *Adjusted net income excludes future pledges, grant-covered start-up costs, interest income, and depreciation.",
  "fin_revmix_note": "<b>The one growing line:</b> digital circulation revenue is <i>up</i> 17.3% YTD (and +29.6% in August) — every print line and digital advertising are down double digits YoY. Digital subscriptions remain the only organic revenue engine that is growing.",
